# nr-office-journal-ledger: what the lead applies (nothing here is a protocol row; no SERVICE_PENDING name changes).

[cargo-lock]
# crate mixdog-office-base got new workspace dependency edges (its own Cargo.toml is already edited). Cargo.lock: in the
# [[package]] entry of "mixdog-office-base", `dependencies` gains
#   "mixdog-fsio", "mixdog-rt", "mixdog-statefile"
# and (dev-dependencies are listed in the same array) "base64", "tempfile", "tokio". All of them are crates already in
# the lock; nothing new is fetched. `mixdog-rt` is used with features test-support + virtual-clock by this crate's tests
# (the same set mixdog-statefile's tests use), `tokio` with feature rt.
# mixdog-workspace-hack/Cargo.toml: re-run cargo hakari generate so tokio/rt, tempfile and base64 are unified for
# mixdog-office-base (a test build only).

[workspace-members]
# no change: mixdog-office-base is already a member; the benchmarks recorder needs no Cargo entry.

[fixtures]
# native/core/fixtures/office-journal/ (golden.json + MANIFEST.json) is added by this task, and native/core/fixtures/MANIFEST.json
# carries the new index entry for set "office-journal" (after "office-detect"). benchmarks/rust-core/recorders/record-office-journal.mjs
# re-records it (and prints `golden.json <n> bytes`); with `--read-dir <dir>` it prints what Node reads from a data dir Rust wrote.

[consumers]
# The seam the engine (mixdog-office, nr-office-*-engine tasks) and the wiring use:
#   mixdog_office_base::ledger::CallLedger::new(cwd, data_dir) -> io::Result<CallLedger>   (impl WriteNote; one per tool call)
#   CallLedger::changes(&proof) -> Vec<FileChange { path: PathBuf, before: ChangeSide, after: ChangeSide }>
#   ChangeSide::{Absent, Bytes(Vec<u8>), Uncaptured { size: u64, reason: Option<String> }}
# mixdog-tools office.rs `WriteReceipt` is built from a FileChange one to one:
#   path = change.path.to_string_lossy(), and ChangeSide::X -> WriteSide::X (identical variants and fields). The lead/wiring
#   task that registers the in-process office service does that conversion (mixdog-tools must not be depended on by
#   mixdog-office-base, so the type lives here and is mapped there).
# mixdog_office_base::journal::{write_office_journal, read_office_journal, remove_office_journal, list_office_journals}
#   serve office.transactions / recover / begin / commit and `office.sweepJournals` (nr-office-ext-router calls
#   list_office_journals(proof, data_dir, true) from a maintenance/durability lane job).
# Every blocking function takes the proof of the lane job it runs in (&InLane<_> or mixdog_fsio::Unlaned in tests); the
# one exception is the WriteNote seam of CallLedger, whose trait method carries no proof: it reads through
# mixdog_fsio::Unlaned, so the engine's writers (which already run inside a lane job) must call note_write from there, or
# use CallLedger::note_write_in(&lane_proof, path) directly.
